      "subject": "feat(skills): edit existing user-authored skills (#66)",
      "body": "* feat(skills): edit existing user-authored skills\n\nAdd `PUT /api/harness/skills/mine/{name}` to rewrite a user-created\nskill's SKILL.md (frontmatter + body). Guards: 404 when the skill is\nmissing, 403 when it isn't user-created, 400 on an invalid name.\nMirrors the create flow's shared frontmatter renderer and its\nharness-first / write-last ordering so the marker-bearing file wins.\n\nFrontend: wire an \"Edit skill\" action in SkillsTab into a repurposed\neditor modal that pre-fills from getSkill, keeps the name read-only,\nand round-trips allowed_tools/model/context so an edit doesn't drop\nfields the UI doesn't surface.\n\nAdds backend handler tests (rewrite+reregister, 404, 403, 400) and\nfrontend tests for the updateMySkill client and the edit wiring.\n\n* fix(skills): fail loud when skill-edit re-register fails\n\nThe skill-edit re-register POST to the harness is what reloads the\nin-memory skill registry, and that registry — not the on-disk file — is\nwhat agents resolve a skill's content from. It was fire-and-forget, so a\nfailed POST left the registry serving the old body while the handler\nstill rewrote SKILL.md and returned 200: a silent stale-serve behind a\nsuccess response.\n\nMake the edit path check the harness response (new post_json_ok gateway\nhelper) and return 502 before writing the file, so a failed re-register\nleaves disk and the live registry consistent (both pre-edit) instead of\ndiverging. Adds a failing-harness mock and a test asserting 502 + the\non-disk file is untouched.",
