      "subject": "fix(billing): retry transient credit pre-flight failures",
      "body": "require_credits called the billing client once with no retry, so a single\ntransport blip or 5xx (e.g. a billing-server cold start) failed the user's\nchat turn outright with a 502. Retry transient failures (transport errors\nand 5xx) with short backoffs; definitive answers (insufficient credits,\nauth/account errors) return immediately without retry, so broke users pay\nno latency penalty. Cache only positive results, since the credit cache is\nread solely as a positive has-credits short-circuit. Adds tests for retry\nrecovery, error-surfaced-without-caching after exhaustion, and\nno-retry-on-insufficient-credits.",
      "parents": [
        "827f924bc5f4a569c4c9bfc02bb6938f738e2385"
